We also define the "BreakLegBalanced" function to extend the leg-balance idea to the breakout itself, measuring the two pattern legs plus the leg from the second peak to the current bar and requiring the shortest of the three to hold up against the longest. This is the optional stricter test that rejects a break arriving too early or too late to sit in proportion with the pattern that produced it.
